        "locator": "approx-hom-pfr-no-const",
        "text": "\\begin{corollary}[Approximate homomorphism form of PFR, no constant term]\\label{approx-hom-pfr-no-const}\\lean{approx_hom_pfr'}\\leanok Let $G,G'$ be finite abelian $2$-groups.\n  Let $f: G \\to G'$ be a function, and suppose that there are at least $|G|^2 / K$ pairs $(x,y) \\in G^2$ such that\n$$ f(x+y) = f(x) + f(y).$$\nThen there exists a homomorphism $\\phi'': G \\to G'$\nsuch that $f(x) = \\phi''(x)$ for at least $(|G| / (2 ^ {172} * K ^ {146}) - 1)/2$ values of $x \\in G$.\n\\end{corollary}",
        "selected": true
      }
    ],
